  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Rhode Island received $658M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state logged 3,928 awards, with an average award size of $167K, and obligations fell 27.4% year over year. The Department of Defense dominated buying, obligating $541M, while the Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Homeland Security followed with $53M and $17.1M respectively. Engineering Services led industry spending at $249M, followed by Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $71.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $56.1M. Top vendors in FY2026 to date included RAYTHEON COMPANY at $81.8M, SEACORP, LLC at $74.3M, and RITE-SOLUTIONS, INC. at $59.4M. Fiscal-year trends show higher totals in recent years such as $1.2B in FY22 and FY24, and a decline from $906M in FY25 to current-year obligations of $658M. These figures are fiscal year to date and represent contract obligations recorded so far in FY2026.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Rhode Island obligations fell 27.4% year over year. FY26 to date obligations stand at $658M compared with $906M in FY25. Prior years included $1.2B in FY24 and $1.2B in FY22, showing that FY26 to date is lower than several recent fiscal years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries drove spending in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $541M in FY2026 to date. Engineering Services is the largest industry, accounting for $249M, followed by Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $71.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $56.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
